experiment: dlvry
  SHORT RUN — 3400000 ticks against a minimum of 27200000.   dirbudget reported its rungs in TICKS and read them as experience. Its
  delivered fraction -- scored, voiced, labelled trials over the nominal
  ticks/kVLTrialTicks -- falls 71.4% -> 35.8% across the ladder, so 8x of
  ticks bought 4.02x of trials. The trial loop is fixed-rate, so that is
  the creature not answering: silent windows, or formants too degenerate
  to score. Two readings the session totals cannot separate -- the
  creature QUIETS as it trains (a decaying curve averaged over a longer
  window, which makes the rotation decline a PRODUCTION story), or a long
  session is uniformly worse (overhead, and the ladder just needs its
  x-axis relabelled). One arm, 12 of dirbudget own creatures, delivery
  counted tenth by tenth; the within-session shape is the measurement.
  Nothing that moves the creature depends on n_trials here, so the first
  N trials ARE a complete N-trial session: the cumulative delivered count
  at each rung must reproduce dirbudget columns bit-identically, which
  is a prediction rather than a fit. Decay, flat, rising and non-monotone
  are all branched on -- dirbudget printed SATURATES over a resolved
  reversal because its outcome space stopped one short of what happened
  Everything below is printed for debugging and is NOT a
  measurement; this run cannot pass whatever it reads.

  instrument        dlvry   trial seed 000000000135f6de   1214 delivered trials per tenth of one session
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)
  INDEX SOURCE 4, inherited from the genome and NOT set by dlvry.
  The index reads the AUDITORY module, so a CtxDrive injected into the
  context module is IGNORED by it -- such an arm is DERIVED, not an
  oracle.
  An "oracle" arm is only an oracle when the drive and the index use the
  SAME module: ctx_match reads 1.000 for a genuine host-written index and
  well below it for a derived one.
  the question      `dirbudget` read its rungs in TICKS and treated them as
                    experience. The delivered fraction falls 71.4% -> 35.8%
                    across that ladder, so 8x of ticks bought 4.02x of
                    trials. The trial loop is fixed-rate, so the deficit is
                    the creature not answering: silence, or formants too
                    degenerate to score.
  the design        ONE arm, 12 creatures, 3400000 ticks = 1214 nominal trials,
                    counted tenth by tenth. No comparison condition is
                    needed: the within-session SHAPE is the measurement.
  the primary       delivered fraction in the LAST tenth minus the FIRST,
                    paired over 12 creatures. DECAY means the creature
                    quiets as it trains and `dirbudget`'s decline is about
                    production, not capacity. FLAT means session overhead
                    and the ladder only needs its x-axis relabelled.
  the prediction    nothing that moves the creature depends on `n_trials`
                    here, so the first N trials of this session ARE a
                    complete N-trial session. The cumulative delivered
                    count at 151 / 303 / 607 / 1214 trials must reproduce
                    `dirbudget`'s 0.425M / 0.85M / 1.7M / 3.4M columns BIT-IDENTICALLY
                    per creature:

                      python3 tools/dlvry_predict.py \
                          results/dirbudget.log <this log>

                    If that fails the rungs are not nested prefixes of one
                    trajectory and this curve says nothing about the
                    shorter budgets.
  what refuses it   a flat per-tenth fraction. Then delivery does not decay
                    with training and reading (a) is dead. RISING and
                    NON-MONOTONE are branched on too -- `dirbudget` printed
                    SATURATES over a resolved reversal because its outcome
                    space stopped one short of what happened.
  stated up front   n = 12, and the per-tenth fraction is a RATIO of two
                    counts, so it is pooled as a ratio of sums and
                    jackknifed, never meaned per creature.

  LIVENESS. 12 of 12 creatures completed the session.

